  "notes": "The sherpa-onnx offline TTS executable runs the Piper VITS voices as a separate process. Piper's own 2023 binaries are x86-64 only on macOS and the maintained piper1-gpl project ships only Python wheels, so the voices are run by sherpa-onnx instead. The voice archives come from the k2-fsa tts-models release (Piper voices converted with tokens and eSpeak NG data). Voices: en_US-ljspeech (public domain dataset) and tr_TR-fettah (CC0 dataset, fine-tuned from the lessac checkpoint). The offline TTS executable statically links eSpeak NG, so it is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later, like the GPL FFmpeg build; the app only starts it as a separate process. Corresponding source: https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/tree/v1.13.8 and https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng.",
